diff --git a/CHANGELOG.en.md b/CHANGELOG.en.md
index 6984b66..b4579ff 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.en.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.en.md
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ Notable changes in Telsiz releases are listed in this file. Version numbers foll
 
 ### Changes
 
-- At medium widths (760 to 1279 pixels) the Stations list shows in the right column above the radio card, so rooms and direct messages are reachable without pressing a button. The list is hidden only on screens shorter than 720 pixels and on phones, and then the Stations button in the top bar shows. On phones the closed radio card no longer has the "Pick a voice room" bar that could not be pressed, and has a 44 pixel Voice Rooms button that opens the Stations sheet at the voice rooms instead. On touch screens room and sheet rows and the buttons of the top bar and the conversation header are at least 44 pixels high. On phones bottom sheets close when dragged down by their handle or header. The unread count at startup comes from the newest 50 messages, so 120 unread messages showed as "50". Now they show as "50+", and the count becomes exact once the conversation is opened.
+- At medium widths (760 to 1279 pixels) the Stations list shows in the right column above the radio card, so rooms and direct messages are reachable without pressing a button. The list is hidden on screens shorter than 720 pixels, on phones and when the radio card grows in a voice room and leaves no room for two rows of the list, and then the Stations button in the top bar shows. On phones the closed radio card no longer has the "Pick a voice room" bar that could not be pressed, and has a 44 pixel Voice Rooms button that opens the Stations sheet at the voice rooms instead. On touch screens room and sheet rows and the buttons of the top bar and the conversation header are at least 44 pixels high. On phones bottom sheets close when dragged down by their handle or header. The unread count at startup comes from the newest 50 messages, so 120 unread messages showed as "50". Now they show as "50+", and the count becomes exact once the conversation is opened.
 - The placeholder of the Add Friend field now reads "Enter a username" (before "username"). The field's label is only visible to screen readers, so the placeholder is the only visible hint.
 - The display name and @username on the profile card now sit to the right of the profile picture, with the role right next to the name. Before, the name, username and role were stacked below the picture. Plain members now also get a faint "Member" badge on their card, and someone with a custom role shows both badges. The My Account and Profile previews in Settings and the head of the avatar menu use the same layout and also show the custom role (the avatar menu used to write the role next to the username). If the name is long the role wraps to the next line, and if the card gets very narrow (for example on a phone with a large font size) the name moves below the picture. On a phone with a large font size the right edge of the card no longer runs off the screen.
 - In every theme text and user interface component colors are now measured on all nine surfaces, hover and selected backgrounds included (`scripts/kontrast.js`, `test/tema.test.js`). Colors that fell slightly below the threshold in this measurement were adjusted: the online and idle markers in Night Frequency light mode and the live color in Turquoise and Copper light mode became slightly darker, and the danger text and the input border in Turquoise and Copper dark mode became slightly lighter. Of the eight custom role colors shared by the light modes, seven became slightly darker and blue stayed the same. The colors of the Camera, Microphone, Deafen and Screen buttons on the radio card now come from tone tokens (`--tone-*`) that themes can override.
